## SKILL DEFINITION FORMAT

### Complete Skill File Structure

```
/skills
  /hvac-diagnostics
    SKILL.md           # Skill documentation
    config.yaml        # Skill configuration
    knowledge/
      ahu_faults.md    # AHU troubleshooting guide
      chiller_faults.md
      refrigerants.md
      manufacturers/
        carrier.md
        trane.md
    workflows/
      ahu_not_cooling.yaml
      chiller_trip.yaml
      high_discharge.yaml
    prompts/
      diagnose.txt
      analyze.txt
```

### SKILL.md Example

```markdown
# HVAC Diagnostics Skill

## Overview
This skill provides expert-level HVAC equipment diagnostics,
combining manufacturer knowledge, fault code interpretation,
and data-driven analysis.

## Capabilities
- Diagnose AHU, chiller, FCU, VAV faults
- Interpret manufacturer fault codes
- Analyze trend data for root cause
- Generate actionable recommendations
- Create work orders for repairs

## Equipment Supported
- Air Handling Units (all types)
- Chillers (scroll, screw, centrifugal, absorption)
- Cooling Towers
- Fan Coil Units
- VAV Boxes
- Heat Pumps
- Pumps (CHW, CW, HW)

## Usage Examples

### Example 1: AHU Not Cooling
User: "AHU-L12-001 is not maintaining temperature"
Skill: Gathers data, analyzes trends, checks recent alarms,
       provides diagnosis with probable causes ranked by likelihood.

### Example 2: Chiller Trip
User: "Why did CH-001 trip?"
Skill: Retrieves fault code, analyzes conditions at time of trip,
       provides diagnosis and recommended actions.

## MCP Tools Used
- get_asset_detail
- get_alarms
- get_trends
- get_work_orders
- create_work_order
```

### config.yaml Example

```yaml
skill:
  id: hvac-diagnostics
  name: HVAC Diagnostics Expert
  version: 1.2.0
  author: SENTINEL Team

  # Activation triggers
  triggers:
    keywords:
      - hvac
      - ahu
      - air handling
      - chiller
      - cooling
      - heating
      - temperature
      - humidity
      - refrigerant
      - compressor

    asset_types:
      - AHU
      - Chiller
      - CoolingTower
      - FCU
      - VAV
      - HeatPump
      - Pump_CHW
      - Pump_CW

    alarm_codes:
      - TEMP_HIGH
      - TEMP_LOW
      - TRIP
      - FREEZE
      - PRESS_HIGH
      - PRESS_LOW
      - FLOW_LOW
      - VIB_HIGH

  # MCP tools this skill can use
  mcp_tools:
    - get_asset_detail
    - get_alarms
    - get_trends
    - get_health_score
    - get_risk_score
    - get_work_orders
    - search_alarms
    - create_work_order

  # Knowledge files to load
  knowledge:
    - knowledge/ahu_faults.md
    - knowledge/chiller_faults.md
    - knowledge/refrigerants.md
    - knowledge/manufacturers/*.md

  # Available workflows
  workflows:
    - id: ahu_not_cooling
      name: AHU Not Cooling Diagnosis
      file: workflows/ahu_not_cooling.yaml

    - id: chiller_trip
      name: Chiller Trip Analysis
      file: workflows/chiller_trip.yaml

    - id: high_discharge
      name: High Discharge Pressure
      file: workflows/high_discharge.yaml

  # Default prompts
  prompts:
    diagnose: prompts/diagnose.txt
    analyze: prompts/analyze.txt
    recommend: prompts/recommend.txt
```

### Workflow Definition Example

```yaml
# workflows/ahu_not_cooling.yaml

workflow:
  id: ahu_not_cooling
  name: AHU Not Cooling Diagnosis
  description: Systematic diagnosis of AHU cooling issues

  inputs:
    - asset_id: required
    - symptoms: optional

  steps:
    - id: gather_data
      name: Gather Asset Data
      actions:
        - tool: get_asset_detail
          params:
            asset_id: "{{asset_id}}"
            include: [health_breakdown, recent_alarms, predictions]

        - tool: get_trends
          params:
            asset_id: "{{asset_id}}"
            parameters: [supply_air_temp, return_air_temp, chw_valve, fan_speed, filter_dp]
            period: 7d

        - tool: get_alarms
          params:
            asset_id: "{{asset_id}}"
            period: 30d

    - id: analyze_symptoms
      name: Analyze Symptoms
      logic: |
        Check supply air temperature vs setpoint
        If SAT > setpoint + 2°C:
          - Cooling capacity issue

        Check CHW valve position:
        If valve = 100%:
          - Maximum demand, check CHW supply
        If valve < 50% and SAT high:
          - Control issue or valve stuck

        Check filter DP:
        If filter_dp > limit:
          - Restricted airflow, filters clogged

        Check fan speed:
        If fan_speed < expected:
          - Fan issue or VSD problem

    - id: determine_causes
      name: Determine Probable Causes
      logic: |
        Rank causes by:
        1. Filter DP high → Clogged filters (common, easy fix)
        2. CHW valve 100% → CHW supply issue
        3. CHW ΔT high → Flow restriction
        4. Fan speed low → VSD or motor issue
        5. Recent similar alarms → Recurring issue

    - id: generate_recommendations
      name: Generate Recommendations
      output:
        diagnosis: "{{diagnosis_text}}"
        probable_causes:
          - cause: "{{cause_1}}"
            likelihood: "{{likelihood_1}}"
            action: "{{action_1}}"
          - cause: "{{cause_2}}"
            likelihood: "{{likelihood_2}}"
            action: "{{action_2}}"
        recommended_action: "{{primary_recommendation}}"
        create_work_order: "{{wo_recommendation}}"
```

