## **Hybrid AI Architecture - Ollama + Claude**

### **Available Models**

**Local (Docker Ollama):**
- ✅ `llama3.2:1b` (1.3 GB) - Fastest for simple tasks
- ✅ `phi3:mini` (2.2 GB) - Balanced performance
- ✅ `nomic-embed-text` (274 MB) - Embeddings

**Cloud (API):**
- ✅ OpenAI (currently configured)
- ✅ Anthropic Claude (can add)

### **Task Routing Strategy**

**TIER 1: Ollama (Local) - FREE** 🆓
```
Simple lookups:
• "What does error E14 mean?"
• "What's the status of AHU-L12-01?"
• "Who stocks Carrier compressors?"
• "List all equipment with health < 70%"

→ Model: llama3.2:1b (50-100ms response)
→ Cost: FREE
→ Usage: ~70% of queries
```

**TIER 2: Claude (Cloud) - Paid** 💰
```
Complex reasoning:
• "Why is the chiller not starting?"
• "Too hot at desk 25" (comfort complaints)
• "Diagnose this unusual pattern"
• "Recommend optimization strategy"

→ Model: claude-sonnet-4 (500ms-1s response)
→ Cost: ~$0.003 per query
→ Usage: ~30% of queries
```

### **Cost Comparison**

**Scenario: 1000 queries/day**

| Approach | Daily Cost | Monthly Cost | Savings |
|----------|-----------|--------------|---------|
| All Claude | $1.50 | $45 | - |
| Hybrid (70/30) | $0.45 | $13.50 | **70%** ✅ |
| All Ollama | $0 | $0 | 100% (but less smart) |

**Recommendation**: Hybrid approach - best of both worlds!

### **Two-Tier Architecture**

```
USER: "Too hot at desk 25"
    ↓
TIER 1: Ollama (llama3.2:1b)
    • Extract desk number
    • Lookup desk→zone mapping
    • Query BMS status
    • Fetch weather data
    • Get time & occupancy
    ↓ (structured data)
TIER 2: Claude (claude-sonnet-4)
    • Analyze all data
    • Identify root cause
    • Generate 3 options
    • Risk assessment
    • Format response
    ↓
USER: "Zone is 23.5°C. Options: A) Boost cooling..."
```

### **Benefits**

✅ **Cost**: 60-70% reduction vs all-cloud
✅ **Speed**: Local responds in 50-100ms
✅ **Privacy**: Sensitive data stays on-prem
✅ **Reliability**: Works offline if internet fails
✅ **Intelligence**: Claude for complex reasoning
✅ **Scalability**: Add more local models as needed

